["Here is a basic implementation of such a function using JavaScript's `MutationObserver` for handling DOM changes and `requestAnimationFrame` for managing concurrency:

```javascript
class DomTraverser {
  constructor(selector, paginationSize = 10) {
    this.selector = selector;
    this.paginationSize = paginationSize;
    this.processedElements = new Set();
    this.observer = null;
    this.queue = [];
    this.isProcessing = false;
  }

  start() {
    const observerCallback = (mutationsList, observer) => {
      for(let mutation of mutationsList) {
        if (mutation.type === 'childList') {
          for(let node of mutation.addedNodes) {
            this.queueNode(node);
          }
        }
      }
    };

    const config = { attributes: false, childList: true, subtree: true };
    this.observer = new MutationObserver(observerCallback);
    this.observer.observe(document, config);
  }

  stop() {
    if (this.observer) {
      this.observer.disconnect();
      this.observer = null;
    }
  }

  queueNode(node) {
    if (!this.processedElements.has(node)) {
      this.queue.push(node);
      this.processQueue();
    }
  }

  processQueue() {
    if (!this.isProcessing && this.queue.length > 0) {
      this.isProcessing = true;
      requestAnimationFrame(() => {
        const chunkSize = Math.min(this.paginationSize, this.queue.length);
        for (let i = 0; i < chunkSize; i++) {
          const node = this.queue.shift();
          if (!this.processedElements.has(node)) {
            this.processNode(node);
            this.processedElements.add(node);
          }
        }
        this.isProcessing = false;
        this.processQueue();
      });
    }
  }

  processNode(node) {
    if (typeof node.querySelectorAll === 'function') {
      const elements = Array.from(node.querySelectorAll(this.selector));
      for (let element of elements) {
        this.processElement(element);
      }
    }
  }

  processElement(element) {
    // Process the element as needed, e.g., update data attributes or styles
    console.log('Processing:', element);
  }
}
```

This code creates a `DomTraverser` class that observes DOM changes and processes elements matching a given selector in chunks using `requestAnimationFrame` for concurrency management. It uses a queue to manage the order of processing, and a set to track already processed nodes to avoid redundant work. 

Please note that this is a basic implementation and may need further optimization or adjustments based on specific requirements and constraints. For example, you might want to add error handling, support for different types of selectors, or integrate with other systems more seamlessly.
"]

