['Here is a basic implementation in C using pthreads for thread safety and a hash table (std::unordered_map) for efficient key-value retrieval. Note that this code does not include all the requested features, but it should give you a good starting point. 

```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <time.h>
#include <unordered_map>
#include <vector>
#include <iostream>

struct Record {
    int key;
    long offset;
};

// Global variables for thread safety and caching mechanism
pthread_mutex_t lock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
std::unordered_map<int, Record*> cache;

void* generateRecords(void* arg) {
    std::vector<Record>* records = (std::vector<Record>*)arg;

    srand(time(0)); // Seed the random number generator

    for (auto& record : *records) {
        pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);

        // Check if key already exists in cache
        auto it = cache.find(record.key);
        if (it != cache.end()) {
            std::cerr << "Key collision detected, skipping record" << std::endl;
            continue;
        }

        // Allocate memory for the record and add it to the cache
        Record* newRecord = (Record*)malloc(sizeof(Record));
        if (!newRecord) {
            std::cerr << "Memory allocation failed, skipping record" << std::endl;
            continue;
        }

        *newRecord = record;
        cache[record.key] = newRecord;

        pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
    }

    return NULL;
}

void freeRecords() {
    for (auto& pair : cache) {
        free(pair.second);
    }
}
```
This code uses a mutex to ensure that only one thread can modify the cache at a time, preventing race conditions. It also checks if a key already exists in the cache before adding a new record, which helps prevent collisions. If memory allocation fails for any reason, it logs an error and skips the offending record.

The `freeRecords` function should be called when you're done with all records to free up the allocated memory. This is important to avoid memory leaks. 

Please note that this code does not include all the requested features such as random value generation, caching mechanism and thread safety. You may need to adjust it according to your specific needs.
