["Here's a Java method that loads a state object from a file using an ObjectInputStream and returns it if it is an instance of the MoSTState class, otherwise null. This method handles exceptions gracefully and ensures proper closure of the ObjectInputStream. 

```java
import java.io.*;

public class StateManager {
    public static Object loadState(String filePath) {
        Object state = null;
        FileInputStream fis = null;
        ObjectInputStream ois = null;

        try {
            fis = new FileInputStream(filePath);
            ois = new ObjectInputStream(fis);

            state = ois.readObject();

            if (!(state instanceof MoSTState)) {
                state = null;
            }
        } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        } finally {
            try {
                if (ois != null) ois.close();
                if (fis != null) fis.close();
            } catch (IOException e) {
                e.printStackTrace();
            }
        }

        return state;
    }
}
```

For the C++ function, we can use a forward list and iterate through it to find the first occurrence of the first string argument. If found, insert the second string after that position. If not found, insert at the end. 

```cpp
#include <forward_list>
#include <string>
using namespace std;

void insertAfter(forward_list<string>& flist, const string& target, const string& toInsert) {
    auto prev = flist.before_begin();
    for (auto it = flist.begin(); it != flist.end(); ++it) {
        if (*it == target) {
            flist.insert_after(it, toInsert);
            return;
        }
        prev = it;
    }

    flist.insert_after(prev, toInsert);
}
```

